7Syntax of JQuery 
The JQuery syntax is based on selecting HTML elements and 
performing some action on that elements. 
▪Basic Syntax: 
•$(selector).action() 
•$-  It is shortcut for JQuery 
•Selector-It is any HTML element in DOM 
•Action-IT is action performed on that element. 
Example: 
$(“button”).click() 
$(“p”),hide() 
$(“h2”).fadeOut() 

--- Page 8 ---
09-03-2025 
Mukti Patel, Dept. of Computer Sc. & 
Engineering 
8Example 
$(this).hide() - hides the current element. 
$("p").hide() - hides all <p> elements. 
$(".test").hide() - hides all elements with 
class="test". 
$("#test").hide() - hides the element with id="test". 


